# Compiled class file
*.class

# Log file
*.log

# BlueJ files
*.ctxt

# Mobile Tools for Java (J2ME)
.mtj.tmp/

# Package Files #
*.jar
*.war
*.nar
*.ear
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.rar

# virtual machine crash logs, see http://www.java.com/en/download/help/error_hotspot.xml
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

# Sweet Home 3D archives — large binaries (127 MB for the four gallery plans).
# Only the extracted Home.xml is tracked; that is the part anything reads, and
# the archives are re-downloadable. See docs/examples/README.md.
panel/tool/fixtures/*.sh3d

# Playwright MCP's scratch output — page snapshots, console logs and traces
# it writes beside the cwd on every navigation (.mcp.json's `playwright`).
# Agent working notes, not artefacts anyone reads twice.
.playwright-mcp/

# Compiled Python bytecode. 61 of these were tracked until 2026-08-09 and are
# now removed — three from `hub/talk-watchdog/` (ours, committed by accident in
# 39c8365) and the rest under `hub/custom_components/`, written by the Home
# Assistant container as **root** while it imports HACS and emporia_vue.
#
# That second group is the reason this rule matters rather than being tidiness:
# `hub/custom_components/` is HA's live config directory, mounted into a
# running container, so the container regenerates these on every start and they
# would otherwise reappear as diff noise for ever. They are also per-interpreter
# (`cpython-312` and `cpython-314` both appeared, from two different Python
# versions touching the same tree), so they churn whenever an image is bumped.
#
# Always regenerable, never read by anything but the interpreter that wrote
# them: every one of the 61 had its `.py` beside it, checked before deleting.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# macOS
.DS_Store
